    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/420765612/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Monday Jan. 14.  95. Lion d’Or. Reims
Still here, and still happy. We have enjoyed the Cathedral  au fond , and each other very much.
Tuesday Jan. 15.  95. Victoria. Bâle
Bernhard and I left at 7.0 in the morning, and HO was going to Paris in the 8.12 train. We came here, reading  La fin du Paganisme (Boissier ) and  James’ Psychology .  Arriving here, we found the line broken by an avalanche, and so have to stay over. 
Wednesday Jan. 16. 95. Bâle
Went to the museum and saw the Böcklins. There are 3 large frescoes on the staircase, which are really  dreadful.  Not only without drawing, but really without """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 86 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1894-95> .

